IMPORT prelude

-- Dental Registration Act 1999 (Singapore) -- who may practise dentistry and use the titles (ss 29, 33, 36, 73, 74), the offences
-- around unlawful practice and the penalty (ss 30-32, 35), titles and specialist claims answerable only in discipline (ss 38, 39),
-- the practising certificate (s 17), temporary registration (s 14B(2)), the Disciplinary Committee's sanctions and when they take
-- effect (ss 50(2), 51(1), (9)-(14)), and composition of offences (s 76).
--
-- Edition: 2022 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/DRA1999.txt, with amendments
-- to S 583/2026 (in force 3 September 2026, the Schedule) and Act 19 of 2025 (in force 5 December 2025, service of documents) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 13 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to what a dentist, an oral health
-- therapist, an employer or a patient actually meets. Not encoded: the Council and its constitution (Part 2), the registers and
-- registration entitlements beyond s 14B(2) (ss 12-16, 18-28), the Accreditation Board (Part 4A), complaints, Health Committee and
-- interim orders procedure (Part 5 apart from ss 50(2), 51), funds, inspectors, regulations, savings, and the Schedule of
-- registrable qualifications. Fraudulent registration (s 34) is covered only through the penalty in s 35.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dental Registration Act 1999 -- practice`

-- The facts about one person at the moment of the act in question.
DECLARE Person HAS
    `is a registered dentist` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a registered oral health therapist` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a practising certificate in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has registration suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acts within the prescribed oral health therapist scope of practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a registered medical practitioner practising medicine or surgery` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an oral health therapist, dental student or medical student in training` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is supervised by a first-division registered dentist` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in a hospital or dental school approved by the Council` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `29, 32, 51(15), 73, 74 -- who may practise dentistry`

-- s 51(15): "While any order of suspension of registration remains in force, the person concerned is not to be regarded as being
-- registered under this Act, even though the person's name still appears in the appropriate register". s 17(7): on suspension "any
-- practising certificate issued to him or her is deemed to be cancelled".
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is effectively a dentist with a practising certificate` IF
        `the person`'s `is a registered dentist`
    AND `the person`'s `has a practising certificate in force`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `has registration suspended`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is effectively an oral health therapist with a practising certificate` IF
        `the person`'s `is a registered oral health therapist`
    AND `the person`'s `has a practising certificate in force`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `has registration suspended`)

-- s 29(1): "Subject to sections 73 and 74, a person must not practise dentistry in Singapore unless the person is a registered
-- dentist and has in force a practising certificate." (2): not a registered oral health therapist with a practising certificate who
-- practises "in accordance with the scope of practice prescribed under section 79". (3): offence.
-- s 73: "Nothing in this Act prevents the practice of medicine or surgery by any medical practitioner registered under the Medical
-- Registration Act 1997." (INFERENCE: the exemption is read as covering the doctor only where the act is the practice of medicine
-- or surgery; the text does not say whether dentistry done by a doctor is always that.)
-- s 74: "any oral health therapist, dental student or medical student" if the act is (a) "in the course of his or her training";
-- (b) "under the supervision of a registered dentist whose name appears in the first division"; and (c) "in a hospital or dental
-- school approved ... by the Council". All three.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may practise dentistry` IF
        `is effectively a dentist with a practising certificate` `the person`
    OR  (`is effectively an oral health therapist with a practising certificate` `the person`
            AND `the person`'s `acts within the prescribed oral health therapist scope of practice`)
    OR  `the person`'s `is a registered medical practitioner practising medicine or surgery`
    OR  (`the person`'s `is an oral health therapist, dental student or medical student in training`
            AND `the person`'s `is supervised by a first-division registered dentist`
            AND `the person`'s `is in a hospital or dental school approved by the Council`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `practising dentistry is an offence under section 29` IF
    NOT `may practise dentistry` `the person`

-- s 32(1): a person whose registration "has been suspended under section 50 or 55 must not practise dentistry during the period of
-- his or her suspension"; (2) offence. A separate offence from s 29 on the same facts.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `practising dentistry is an offence under section 32` IF
    `the person`'s `has registration suspended`

§§ `30 -- liability of employer, principal or partner`

-- s 30(1): where an s 29 offence is committed by "any person acting as an employee, an agent or a partner of another person, that
-- other person shall also be guilty". (2): a defence "if the defendant proves that the firstmentioned offence was committed without
-- the defendant's knowledge AND that the defendant took reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence". Both limbs.
GIVEN `employee committed a section 29 offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved it was without knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved reasonable precautions and due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is guilty under section 30` IF
        `employee committed a section 29 offence`
    AND (NOT (`proved it was without knowledge` AND `proved reasonable precautions and due diligence`))

§§ `31 -- dentists and oral health therapists who allow unlawful practice`

-- s 31(1): allowing a person to practise in contravention of s 29 "on any premises used by or under the control of" the
-- practitioner. (2): "by his or her presence, countenance, advice, assistance or cooperation, has knowingly enabled" it.
-- (3): "In any proceedings for an offence under subsection (1) or (2)" a defence: (a) mistake, reliance on information, the act of
-- another or a cause beyond control; AND (b) all reasonable precautions and due diligence.
-- (4): practising "on any premises on which any person practises dentistry in contravention of section 29, knowing or having
-- reason to believe" it. The s 31(3) defence is NOT given for subsection (4).
DECLARE Allowing IS ONE OF
    `allowed it on own premises`
    `knowingly enabled it`
    `practised alongside it knowing`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS AN Allowing, `proved mistake or cause beyond control` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved all reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the practitioner is guilty under section 31` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `practised alongside it knowing` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOT (`proved mistake or cause beyond control` AND `proved all reasonable precautions`)

§§ `33 -- titles`

-- s 33(1): a person "other than a registered dentist who has in force a practising certificate" must not take or use (a) "dentist,
-- dental surgeon, registered dentist, qualified dentist, doctor of dental surgery, professor of dentistry or surgeon dentist";
-- (b) a prescribed title; (c) "any name, title, addition or description implying ... that that person is qualified to heal or treat
-- dental disorders or derangement". (2): a person "other than a registered oral health therapist who has in force a practising
-- certificate" must not take or use (a) "oral health therapist"; or (b) the same implying description. (3): offence.
-- READ LITERALLY, the implying description is barred by (1)(c) to everyone but a dentist with a practising certificate, and by
-- (2)(b) to everyone but an oral health therapist with one; only a person who is both escapes both. Encoded literally.
DECLARE Title IS ONE OF
    `dentist`
    `dental surgeon`
    `doctor of dental surgery`
    `professor of dentistry`
    `oral health therapist`
    `a description implying qualification to treat dental disorders`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the title` IS A Title
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may use the title` IF
    CONSIDER `the title`
    WHEN `oral health therapist` THEN `is effectively an oral health therapist with a practising certificate` `the person`
    WHEN `a description implying qualification to treat dental disorders` THEN
            `is effectively a dentist with a practising certificate` `the person`
        AND `is effectively an oral health therapist with a practising certificate` `the person`
    OTHERWISE `is effectively a dentist with a practising certificate` `the person`

§§ `35, 17(8) -- penalties`

-- s 35: an offence under s 29, 30, 31, 32, 33 or 34: "a fine not exceeding $25,000 and, in the case of a second or subsequent
-- conviction ... a fine not exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both."
-- s 17(8): failing to surrender a deemed-cancelled practising certificate: "a fine not exceeding $1,000".
GIVEN `previous convictions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 35` MEANS
    IF `previous convictions` AT LEAST 1 THEN 50000 ELSE 25000

GIVEN `previous convictions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months under section 35` MEANS
    IF `previous convictions` AT LEAST 1 THEN 6 ELSE 0

§§ `36 -- recovering fees`

-- s 36(1): no one may "demand, claim, accept, receive, retain or sue for or recover any fee" for an act within the practice of
-- dentistry "unless, at the time of carrying out the act, the person is registered as a dentist or an oral health therapist under
-- this Act and has in force a practising certificate". (2): not "any medical practitioner registered under the Medical Registration
-- Act 1997". The oral health therapist's scope of practice is not a condition here. Suspension is read through s 51(15).
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `is a registered medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may charge a fee for the dental act` IF
        `is a registered medical practitioner`
    OR  `is effectively a dentist with a practising certificate` `the person`
    OR  `is effectively an oral health therapist with a practising certificate` `the person`

§§ `38 -- designations a registered dentist may use (discipline, not offence)`

-- s 38(2): a dentist in the FIRST division "must not use any title, addition or designation other than (a) the title, addition or
-- designation which has been approved by the Council for his or her use; or (b)" a prescribed title for which he or she is listed.
-- (3): a dentist in the SECOND division must not use any other than "registered dentist", "dentist" or a listed prescribed title.
-- (4): contravention "may be subject to disciplinary proceedings" and "is deemed to be an act which brings disrepute".
DECLARE Division IS ONE OF
    `first division`
    `second division`

DECLARE Designation IS ONE OF
    `the designation dentist`
    `the designation registered dentist`
    `the designation dental surgeon`
    `a prescribed title`

GIVEN `the division` IS A Division, `the designation` IS A Designation, `approved by the Council` IS A BOOLEAN, `on the prescribed list` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may use the designation` IF
    CONSIDER `the division`
    WHEN `first division` THEN
            `approved by the Council`
        OR  (`the designation` EQUALS `a prescribed title` AND `on the prescribed list`)
    WHEN `second division` THEN
            `the designation` EQUALS `the designation dentist`
        OR  `the designation` EQUALS `the designation registered dentist`
        OR  (`the designation` EQUALS `a prescribed title` AND `on the prescribed list`)

§§ `39 -- holding out as a specialist (discipline, not offence)`

-- s 39(1): a registered dentist "who is not registered under section 14C as a specialist" in a branch must not practise under the
-- title of a specialist in it, or "advertise or hold himself or herself out as a specialist". (2): "may be subject to disciplinary
-- proceedings". s 50(1)(e) lists contravening s 38 or 39 as a ground for the Disciplinary Committee. Neither s 38 nor s 39 is in
-- the s 35 list of offences.
GIVEN `held out as a specialist` IS A BOOLEAN, `registered as a specialist in that branch` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exposed to discipline under section 39` IF
    `held out as a specialist` AND (NOT `registered as a specialist in that branch`)

GIVEN `the section` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section is an offence penalised by section 35` IF
    `the section` AT LEAST 29 AND `the section` AT MOST 34

§§ `17, 14B(2) -- practising certificate and temporary registration`

-- s 17(3): a practising certificate "for a period not exceeding 2 years from the date of issue". (4): renewal "not later than one
-- month before the expiry"; (5): a later applicant "is liable to pay ... such late application fee as may be prescribed".
-- s 14B(2): temporary registration "for a period not exceeding 3 years which may be renewed, at the discretion of the Council".
GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the practising certificate period is within section 17(3)` IF
    `months` GREATER THAN 0 AND `months` AT MOST 24

GIVEN `days before expiry when applying` IS A NUMBER, `one month in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a late application fee is payable` IF
    `days before expiry when applying` LESS THAN `one month in days`

GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the temporary registration period is within section 14B(2)` IF
    `months` GREATER THAN 0 AND `months` AT MOST 36

-- s 17(7): on removal from the register or suspension "any practising certificate issued to him or her is deemed to be cancelled
-- and the registered dentist must immediately surrender the certificate". (8): failing to comply is an offence ($1,000).
GIVEN `removed or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN, `surrendered the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to surrender is an offence under section 17(8)` IF
    `removed or suspended` AND (NOT `surrendered the certificate`)

§§ `50(2), 51(1) -- the Disciplinary Committee's sanctions`

-- s 50(2): (b) suspension "for a period of at least 3 months and not more than 3 years"; (c) conditions "for a period not exceeding
-- 3 years"; (d) "a penalty not exceeding $50,000". s 51(1)(b): for breach of conditions, suspension "for any period not exceeding
-- 12 months" -- no minimum is stated.
DECLARE Sanction HAS
    `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER
    `months of conditions` IS A NUMBER
    `penalty` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the sanction` IS A Sanction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sanction is within section 50(2)` IF
        (`the sanction`'s `months of suspension` EQUALS 0
            OR (`the sanction`'s `months of suspension` AT LEAST 3 AND `the sanction`'s `months of suspension` AT MOST 36))
    AND `the sanction`'s `months of conditions` AT MOST 36
    AND `the sanction`'s `penalty` AT MOST 50000

GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension for breach of conditions is within section 51(1)` IF
    `months` GREATER THAN 0 AND `months` AT MOST 12

§§ `51(9)-(14) -- when a disciplinary order takes effect`

-- s 51(9): an order "for the removal of any name or for suspension of registration ... does not take effect until the expiry of 30
-- days after the order is made". (10): the Committee may order immediate effect "for the protection of members of the public or ...
-- in the best interests of" the practitioner; (11) if the person "was present or represented", from the time the order is made;
-- (12) otherwise "from the time of service of the notice". (13): any other order "takes effect from the time the order is made".
-- (14): "Despite anything in this section", where the practitioner has appealed, the order "does not take effect unless the order is
-- confirmed ... or the appeal is ... dismissed ... or is withdrawn". Read literally, (14) also holds back an immediate order.
-- INFERENCE: "the expiry of 30 days after the order is made" is taken as 30 whole days having elapsed.
DECLARE OrderKind IS ONE OF
    `removal or suspension`
    `other order`

DECLARE Order HAS
    `kind` IS AN OrderKind
    `days since made` IS A NUMBER
    `ordered to take effect immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
    `present or represented` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice served` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appealed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appeal disposed of against the practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order is in effect` IF
        ((NOT `the order`'s `appealed`) OR `the order`'s `appeal disposed of against the practitioner`)
    AND `timing is satisfied` `the order`

GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `timing is satisfied` IF
    CONSIDER `the order`'s `kind`
    WHEN `other order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `removal or suspension` THEN
        IF `the order`'s `ordered to take effect immediately`
        THEN (`the order`'s `present or represented` OR `the order`'s `notice served`)
        ELSE `the order`'s `days since made` AT LEAST 30

§§ `76 -- composition`

-- s 76(1): the Council may compound a prescribed compoundable offence "by collecting ... a sum not exceeding the lower of the
-- following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; or (b) $500."
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 500
